Z||000032||Oreif||12-14-2001||10:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Screwie:<BR><B>Us guys and girls who have been born in 1980 have it really easy! How old am I again? Well, in let's say 2023, we will be 20+23=43! In 2054 we will be 20+54=74   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Yeah being born in 1980 rulezz!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You do realize you were only 3 years old when Fiero's came out. I on the other hand was 20 and able to test drive a brand new 1984 Fiero SE at the dealership.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>(8May63)<BR><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000033||Formula88||12-14-2001||10:31 AM||||Good point, Orief!  I graduated High School in 1983.  No, I didn't get a Fiero, but that Fall, I could go test drive them.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I still remember my first test drive in a GT.  It was an '88 Automatic, Bright Red with a Beechwood interior.  MAN that thing cornered like no car I'd ever been in!  Awesome.  I almost bought it, too, but I was a straight line gearhead and wanted more power.  So I went with an '87 Grand National instead.  It was a toss-up between that or an 88 Formula 350 Firebird, but since a friend of mine bought a GN, I couldn't buy something <I>slower</I> now could I?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh, almost forgot (I do that when I start babbling):  <B>06-22-1965</B>||||reg||10
